# cosim_e2e_counter.golden -- the golden for H2, tests/headless/test_cosim_golden_e2e.tcl
# doc/claude/specs/mixed_signal_signal_browser.md section H, item H2.
#
# WHAT THIS IS. Every TRANSITION of the six INTERNAL signals of
# xschem_libraries_oa/ngspice_verilog_cosim_ase/counter/verilog/counter.v, as
# the patched d_cosim shim dumps them, read back through `xschem raw` from the
# VCD produced by a real mixed-signal run of tb_counter_wrapper.
#
# The six are internal on purpose: only module PORTS cross the d_cosim boundary
# (spec M6), so `phase`, `half`, `prev`, `next_count`, `tc` and `carry` exist in
# NO `.raw` file anywhere. They are the payload the Signal Browser work exists
# to show, and a golden made of ports would prove nothing about the VCD.
#
# PROVENANCE, and how to regenerate. Produced 2026-08-11 by the run the test
# itself performs, in the SHIPPING configuration:
#   * build:   tools/cosim/build_cosim_so.sh -V (trace, and NO -t: nothing in
#              src/ase.tcl ever passes -t -- batch F item 12, commit 1e5c2b64),
#              verilator 5.020, g++ 13.3
#   * deck:    xschem netlist of
#              xschem_libraries_oa/ngspice_verilog_cosim_ase/tb_counter_wrapper,
#              rendered by ase::backend::ngspice::render_deck from that cell's
#              own ngspice_state1 state -- VDD 1.8, `tran 10p 2u`, the state's
#              two auto_bridge pre_sets
#   * run:     ngspice-46 -b, cwd = the run directory
# Regenerate by re-running the test and pasting the measured records; do NOT
# hand-edit a time.
#
# STABILITY. Two independent ngspice invocations (`tran 10p 2u` and a truncated
# `tran 10p 400n`) produced byte-identical VCD prefixes, so these numbers are
# the simulator's, not a race. The 1 ps ladder around each clock edge
# (...011 / ...012) is the dac_bridge t_rise=1e-11 plus the shim's event-time
# dump, i.e. physical -- see the A6 row of the spec.
#
# FORMAT.  edge <signal> <time_ps> <value>
# `#` comments and blank lines ignored. Buses carry their decimal value.
#
edge TOP.counter.phase 0 0
edge TOP.counter.phase 50012 1
edge TOP.counter.phase 150012 2
